# THE DEFAULT, AND WHY IT IS FIRST. Later rules win in this file, so this is the baseline every rule
# below deliberately overrides. Without it, a file matching none of them is translated by whatever
# `core.autocrlf` the cloning machine happens to have — which makes the bytes a consumer reads a
# property of the developer rather than of this repository. That is not a style preference:
# test/adapter-policy-binding.test.mjs once extracted a function body with `indexOf("\n}\n")`, got -1
# on a CRLF checkout, and scanned an empty string while reporting success. Repairing that consumer
# did not remove the condition — any later test comparing committed text against generated text can
# acquire the same fault, and it presents as a Windows-only failure a Linux run reports green.
# test/checkout-line-endings.test.mjs holds this file to that invariant.
#
# This does not rewrite a checkout that already exists. Refresh one with:
#     git rm --cached -r . && git reset --hard
* text=auto eol=lf

# The CI container executes ci/checks.sh directly. A CRLF checkout on a Windows developer machine
# makes the shebang unparseable inside a Linux container, and the failure ("bad interpreter") names
# neither the file nor the cause. These line endings are therefore not a style preference.
*.sh            text eol=lf
ci/checks.sh    text eol=lf

# PowerShell is invoked by the host shell, which is fine with either, but keeping the platform
# convention avoids a whole-file diff the first time somebody edits one in a Windows editor.
*.ps1           text eol=crlf

# Generated renders of docs/*.mmd. Marked binary so a diff does not bury a review in path data.
*.svg           -text

# Externally produced evidence, copied verbatim from a named producer commit. `-text` disables all
# line-ending translation, so a Windows checkout cannot rewrite bytes this repository did not author.
# test/fixtures/governance/PROVENANCE.md claims these are byte-for-byte; without this, that claim
# quietly stops being true on every machine that checks out with autocrlf.
test/fixtures/governance/*.json  -text
